  // item win the card.
  // ORDER MATTERS. The picture produced for THIS run (a freshly generated or freshly gated
  // search image) is the best one, because it was chosen with the current rules. A picture saved
  // on the catalogue row comes last: the row still holds whatever the previous run wrote, so
  // putting it first is what kept printing the old bad images on the shop even after the
  // generator had produced a good picture.
  // A picture the MERCHANT sent for this item outranks anything found by search, generated, or
  // stored on a previous card - they chose it themselves and must be able to win with it.
  // A picture is only this card's when we can say WHERE it came from: the picture produced for
  // this run (searched or generated), the merchant's own hosted upload, a real product photo the
  // shop already had, or the photo carried in with this message. A URL the MODEL typed from memory
